"""Crea el proyecto gesture-control: carpetas y todos los archivos.

Uso:  python crear_proyecto.py [carpeta_destino]     (por defecto ./gesture-control)
No sobrescribe archivos que ya existan.
"""
import sys
from pathlib import Path

DIRS = ['config', 'data/raw_videos', 'data/landmarks', 'data/splits', 'models', 'runtime', 'scripts', 'src/gesture_control']

FILES = {
    '.gitignore': '.venv/\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\ndata/landmarks/\ndata/raw_videos/\ndata/splits/\nmodels/\nruntime/\n',
    'README.md': '# Gesture Control\n\nControla ventanas con **gestos de una mano en movimiento**, vistos por la cámara del equipo.\nFunciona en Linux y Windows. Un proceso en segundo plano (el *demonio*) mantiene la cámara abierta y\nejecuta las acciones; un panel Tkinter sirve para grabar, entrenar, probar y encender/apagar el demonio,\ncomo la app de un *live wallpaper*: la cierras y el demonio sigue corriendo.\n\n## Cómo funciona\n\n```\ncámara ─► MediaPipe (21 puntos de la mano) ─► ventana deslizante de ~1.5 s\n        ─► normalización ─► red Conv1D+GRU (TensorFlow) ─► gesto + confianza\n        ─► filtros (umbral, votos, cooldown) ─► acción (Alt+Tab, Alt+F4, …)\n```\n\nNo se entrena sobre píxeles sino sobre **landmarks**: es más ligero, no depende del fondo ni de la luz\ny necesita pocos datos. Los videos se usan igual (se convierten a landmarks).\n\n| Gesto | Acción por defecto |\n|---|---|\n| `swipe_derecha` | Siguiente ventana (Alt+Tab; los swipes seguidos encadenan sin soltar Alt) |\n| `swipe_izquierda` | Ventana anterior (Alt+Shift+Tab) |\n| `swipe_arriba` | Vista general / escritorio |\n| `swipe_abajo` | Minimizar ventana activa |\n| `agarrar` (palma abierta → puño) | Cerrar ventana (Alt+F4) — exige más confianza y un voto extra |\n| `ninguno` | No hace nada (movimiento normal de la mano; **es la clase que evita falsos positivos**) |\n\n## Estructura\n\n```\ngesture-control/\n├── app.py                    # abre el panel\n├── requirements.txt\n├── config/\n│   ├── settings.yaml         # cámara, umbrales, duración de clips, épocas…\n│   └── actions.yaml          # gesto -> acción, y comando por sistema operativo\n├── data/\n│   ├── raw_videos/<gesto>/   # videos opcionales (.mp4 .avi .mov .mkv .webm)\n│   ├── landmarks/<gesto>/    # clips .npz (los crea record.py / import_videos.py)\n│   └── splits/splits.json    # qué clip va a train / val / test\n├── models/                   # modelo .keras, labels, curvas, matriz de confusión\n├── runtime/                  # pid, estado, log del demonio\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── record.py             # graba clips con la cámara\n│   ├── import_videos.py      # videos -> landmarks\n│   ├── build_dataset.py      # divide train/val/test\n│   ├── train.py              # entrena\n│   ├── test.py               # evalúa en test\n│   ├── pipeline.py           # importar -> dataset -> entrenar -> testear\n│   └── run.py                # el demonio\n└── src/gesture_control/      # paths, features, hands, actions, model, gui, daemon…\n```\n\nTodas las rutas se calculan desde la raíz del proyecto (`pathlib`), nada es absoluto.\n\n## 1. Crear carpetas y archivos (solo si no usas el zip)\n\nLa forma más corta: ejecuta `python crear_proyecto.py`, que crea todo el árbol y escribe todos los archivos.\nA mano, solo el esqueleto:\n\n**Linux / macOS**\n```bash\nmkdir -p gesture-control/{config,data/{raw_videos,landmarks,splits},models,runtime,scripts,src/gesture_control}\ncd gesture-control\ntouch app.py requirements.txt .gitignore config/{settings,actions}.yaml\ntouch scripts/{record,import_videos,build_dataset,train,test,pipeline,run}.py\ntouch src/gesture_control/{__init__,paths,config,osinfo,features,camera,hands,actions,model,dataset,training,evaluation,status,daemon,gui}.py\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell)**\n```powershell\n$d = "data\\raw_videos","data\\landmarks","data\\splits","models","runtime","scripts","config","src\\gesture_control"\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (@("gesture-control") + ($d | % { "gesture-control\\$_" })) | Out-Null\ncd gesture-control\n"app.py","requirements.txt",".gitignore","config\\settings.yaml","config\\actions.yaml" | % { New-Item -ItemType File -Force $_ | Out-Null }\n"record","import_videos","build_dataset","train","test","pipeline","run" | % { New-Item -ItemType File -Force "scripts\\$_.py" | Out-Null }\n"__init__","paths","config","osinfo","features","camera","hands","actions","model","dataset","training","evaluation","status","daemon","gui" | % { New-Item -ItemType File -Force "src\\gesture_control\\$_.py" | Out-Null }\n```\n\n## 2. Entorno virtual e instalación\n\nPython 3.10–3.13. Si TensorFlow no publica rueda para tu versión de Python, usa 3.12 (con `uv`, `pyenv` o el\npaquete de tu distro).\n\nTkinter viene aparte en Linux: `sudo pacman -S tk` (Arch) · `sudo apt install python3-tk` (Debian/Ubuntu) ·\n`sudo dnf install python3-tkinter` (Fedora).\n\n**Linux / macOS**\n```bash\ncd gesture-control\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npython -m pip install --upgrade pip\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython app.py\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell)**\n```powershell\ncd gesture-control\npy -3.12 -m venv .venv\n.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1     # si lo bloquea: Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope CurrentUser RemoteSigned\npython -m pip install --upgrade pip\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython app.py\n```\n\nLa primera vez que se usa la mano, se descarga `models/hand_landmarker.task` (de Google). Si no hay\ninternet, descárgalo manualmente de\n`https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/hand_landmarker/hand_landmarker/float16/1/hand_landmarker.task`\ny guárdalo con ese nombre en `models/`.\n\n> MediaPipe eliminó `mediapipe.solutions` en versiones recientes; este proyecto usa solo la API *Tasks*\n> (`HandLandmarker`), que funciona en las versiones nuevas.\n\n## 3. Uso paso a paso\n\nAbre el panel con `python app.py`. Arriba aparece **LISTO** (verde) o **FALTA: …** (rojo), con el detalle de\nqué falta: clips por gesto, videos sin importar, división train/val/test, modelo y test. Los botones siguen\nel orden del flujo:\n\n1. **Grabar datos** (`scripts/record.py`). Se abre la cámara con el esqueleto de la mano dibujado.\n   `1`–`6` elige el gesto, `ESPACIO` graba un clip (cuenta 3-2-1 y 1.5 s), `U` deshace el último,\n   `V` guarda también el video `.mp4`, `Q` sale.\n2. **Importar videos** (opcional). Pon videos en `data/raw_videos/<gesto>/`. Un video corto cuenta como\n   un clip; uno largo se corta en trozos de 1.5 s (ideal para `ninguno`).\n3. **Construir dataset** (`build_dataset.py`). Divide en train/val/test **por sesión de grabación** para\n   que el test mida generalización real y no memoria.\n4. **Entrenar** (`train.py`). Aumenta datos (ruido, escala, rotación leve, recortes de tiempo), usa\n   *early stopping* y guarda el modelo.\n5. **Testear** (`test.py`). Accuracy, reporte por clase y matriz de confusión (pestaña *Gráficas*).\n   **Pipeline 2→5** encadena los pasos 2 a 5.\n\nTodo también funciona por terminal: `python scripts/record.py`, `python scripts/pipeline.py --skip-import`, etc.\n\n### Cuántos datos\n\n- Mínimo 30 clips por gesto (configurable), mejor 60–100. Para `ninguno`, el doble.\n- Graba en **al menos 3 sesiones separadas** (cierra y vuelve a abrir el grabador): cada apertura es una\n  sesión. Con menos de 3 sesiones por gesto, el split usa bloques cronológicos, que protege menos.\n- Varía distancia a la cámara, velocidad, iluminación y fondo. En `ninguno` incluye la mano quieta,\n  mover el mouse, teclear, gesticular al hablar, rascarse… lo que harás mientras el demonio corre.\n- Si cambias `camera.mirror` después de grabar, los swipes izquierda/derecha quedan invertidos: regraba.\n\n## 4. El demonio (modo *live wallpaper*)\n\nEn el panel: **▶ Iniciar demonio** (necesita un modelo entrenado). Puedes cerrar la ventana; el demonio sigue\nen segundo plano con la cámara abierta. Vuelve a abrir `python app.py` para ver su estado o detenerlo.\n\n- **Dry-run**: detecta y muestra la acción sin ejecutarla. Se puede conmutar con el demonio en marcha.\n  Recomendado para probar. El último gesto y la acción aparecen en el panel y en `runtime/daemon.log`.\n- **Ventana de cámara**: muestra la cámara con el esqueleto (útil para depurar; `Q` la cierra).\n- Línea de comandos: `python scripts/run.py [--dry-run] [--preview] [--background]`,\n  `python scripts/run.py --status`, `python scripts/run.py --stop`.\n- Mientras el demonio usa la cámara no se puede grabar; el panel te pide detenerlo antes.\n- **Iniciar con la sesión**: Linux, añade `python /ruta/scripts/run.py --background` (con el python del\n  `.venv`) a *Autostart*. Windows, un `.bat` con ese comando en `shell:startup`.\n\n### Seguridad contra falsos positivos\n\nUmbral de confianza (0.85; 0.95 para cerrar), 2 predicciones iguales seguidas (3 para cerrar), *cooldown* de\n1 s tras cada acción y mínimo de frames con mano en la ventana. Todo en `config/settings.yaml`.\n\n## 5. Linux: X11, Wayland, KDE\n\n`osinfo` detecta el sistema y la sesión, y el panel muestra el backend elegido.\n\n- **X11**: `pynput` funciona. Para minimizar instala `xdotool`.\n- **Wayland** (por defecto en Plasma 6): `pynput` **no puede inyectar teclas**. Opciones:\n  1. Iniciar sesión en X11.\n  2. `ydotool`: instálalo, ten `ydotoold` corriendo y permiso sobre `/dev/uinput`\n     (en Arch: `sudo pacman -S ydotool`, y activa su servicio; revisa la doc de tu distro).\n     Con `backend: auto` se elige solo si está en el PATH.\n  3. Para minimizar en KDE Wayland se usa `kdotool` (AUR). Si tu versión nombra distinto el comando,\n     edítalo en `config/actions.yaml`.\n- La vista general usa `meta+w` (KDE). En GNOME, cámbialo a `meta` en `actions.yaml`.\n\n## 6. Windows\n\n`pynput` funciona directo. Vista general = `win+tab`, minimizar = `win+down` (en una ventana maximizada la\nprimera vez solo la restaura), cerrar = `alt+f4`.\n\n## 7. Personalizar\n\n- **Acciones**: pestaña *Acciones* del panel (edita `config/actions.yaml`). Tipos: `keys: "ctrl+shift+m"`,\n  `alt_tab: forward|backward`, `cmd: "comando externo"`. Cada acción puede definirse por `windows`, `linux`,\n  `linux_wayland` o `all`.\n- **Ajustes**: pestaña *Configuración* (cambia solo los valores, conserva los comentarios del YAML).\n  Cambiar la duración del clip exige regrabar y reentrenar.\n- **Gestos nuevos**: añade el nombre en `gestures:` de `settings.yaml` y en `gestures:` de `actions.yaml`,\n  graba clips y reentrena. El modelo se reentrena desde cero.\n\n## 8. Problemas comunes\n\n| Síntoma | Qué revisar |\n|---|---|\n| No abre la cámara | `camera.index` en `settings.yaml`; cierra otras apps que la usen |\n| No se descarga el modelo de manos | Ver el enlace manual en la sección 2 |\n| Dispara sin querer | Más clips de `ninguno`, subir `threshold` y `votes` |\n| No dispara | Revisa en dry-run con la ventana de cámara que la mano se detecta; baja `threshold`; más datos |\n| Alt+Tab no hace nada en Linux | Casi seguro Wayland sin `ydotool` (el panel muestra una advertencia) |\n| La accuracy de test es mucho menor que la de validación | Pocas sesiones de grabación: graba en más sesiones y condiciones |\n',
    'app.py': '"""Abre el panel de control. Uso:  python app.py"""\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "src"))\n\nfrom gesture_control.gui import main  # noqa: E402\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n',
    'config/actions.yaml': 'gestures:                 # gesto -> acción\n  swipe_derecha: next_window\n  swipe_izquierda: prev_window\n  swipe_arriba: overview\n  swipe_abajo: minimize\n  agarrar: close_window\n\n# Cada acción puede definirse por sistema. Orden de búsqueda:\n#   linux_wayland (solo en Wayland) -> windows | linux -> all\n# Tipos:  keys: "alt+f4"  |  alt_tab: forward/backward  |  cmd: "comando externo"\nactions:\n  next_window:\n    all: {alt_tab: forward}\n  prev_window:\n    all: {alt_tab: backward}\n  overview:\n    windows: {keys: "win+tab"}\n    linux: {keys: "meta+w"}            # KDE Plasma: Vista general. En GNOME usa "meta"\n  minimize:\n    windows: {keys: "win+down"}        # en ventana maximizada, la primera vez solo la restaura\n    linux: {cmd: "xdotool getactivewindow windowminimize"}         # X11 (sudo pacman -S xdotool)\n    linux_wayland: {cmd: "kdotool getactivewindow windowminimize"}  # KDE Wayland (kdotool)\n  close_window:\n    windows: {keys: "alt+f4"}\n    linux: {keys: "alt+f4"}\n',
    'config/settings.yaml': '# Gesture Control - configuración (editable a mano o desde la interfaz)\nsystem:\n  backend: auto            # auto | pynput | ydotool   (auto: Wayland -> ydotool, resto -> pynput)\ncamera:\n  index: 0\n  width: 640\n  height: 480\n  mirror: true             # vista tipo espejo: swipe derecha = mano hacia la derecha\nsequence:\n  clip_seconds: 1.5        # duración de cada clip y de la ventana de análisis en vivo\n  steps: 30                # pasos tras remuestrear (entrada del modelo)\ngestures:\n  - swipe_derecha\n  - swipe_izquierda\n  - swipe_arriba\n  - swipe_abajo\n  - agarrar\n  - ninguno\ndataset:\n  min_clips_per_gesture: 30\n  min_valid_ratio: 0.6     # mínimo de frames con mano detectada para aceptar un clip\n  val_ratio: 0.15\n  test_ratio: 0.15\n  seed: 42\ntraining:\n  epochs: 60\n  batch_size: 32\n  aug_factor: 8            # copias aumentadas por clip de entrenamiento\ninference:\n  predict_every: 3         # predecir cada N frames\n  threshold: 0.85\n  destructive_threshold: 0.95\n  votes: 2                 # predicciones consecutivas iguales antes de actuar (+1 en acciones destructivas)\n  cooldown: 1.0            # segundos entre acciones\n  min_hand_ratio: 0.7      # mínimo de frames con mano en la ventana para predecir\n  alt_hold_seconds: 1.2    # tiempo que se mantiene Alt pulsado para encadenar swipes\n',
    'requirements.txt': 'tensorflow>=2.16\nmediapipe>=0.10.14\nopencv-python>=4.9\nnumpy>=1.26\nscikit-learn>=1.4\nmatplotlib>=3.8\npynput>=1.7.6\nPyYAML>=6.0\npsutil>=5.9\n',
    'scripts/build_dataset.py': '"""Construye data/splits/splits.json (train/val/test por sesión de grabación)."""\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "src"))\n\nfrom gesture_control.config import load_settings  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.dataset import build_splits  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.paths import ensure_dirs  # noqa: E402\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    s = load_settings()\n    ensure_dirs(s["gestures"])\n    report = build_splits(s)\n    print(f"{\'gesto\':<18}{\'clips\':>6}{\'train\':>7}{\'val\':>6}{\'test\':>6}  modo")\n    for g, r in report.items():\n        print(f"{g:<18}{r[\'clips\']:>6}{r[\'train\']:>7}{r[\'val\']:>6}{r[\'test\']:>6}  {r[\'mode\']}")\n    low = [g for g, r in report.items() if min(r["train"], r["val"], r["test"]) < 1]\n    if low:\n        print(f"\\nAviso: sin datos suficientes para train/val/test en: {\', \'.join(low)}")\n',
    'scripts/import_videos.py': '"""Extrae landmarks de videos en data/raw_videos/<gesto>/ y los guarda como clips.\n\nUn video corto (<= ~2.4 s) es un clip. Uno largo se corta en segmentos de clip_seconds\n(útil para \'ninguno\': movimiento normal de la mano).\n"""\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "src"))\n\nimport cv2  # noqa: E402\nimport numpy as np  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom gesture_control.config import load_settings  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.features import RAW_DIM, valid_mask  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.hands import HandTracker  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.paths import LANDMARKS, ensure_dirs  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.status import VIDEO_EXT  # noqa: E402\n\n\ndef extract(video, mirror):\n    cap = cv2.VideoCapture(str(video))\n    fps = cap.get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FPS) or 30.0\n    tracker = HandTracker()  # uno por video: los timestamps deben empezar de cero\n    lms, ts, i = [], [], 0\n    zeros = np.zeros(RAW_DIM, np.float32)\n    try:\n        while True:\n            ok, frame = cap.read()\n            if not ok:\n                break\n            if mirror:\n                frame = cv2.flip(frame, 1)\n            lm = tracker.process(frame, i / fps * 1000)\n            lms.append(lm if lm is not None else zeros)\n            ts.append(i / fps)\n            i += 1\n    finally:\n        cap.release()\n        tracker.close()\n    return (np.stack(lms), np.array(ts)) if lms else (None, None)\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="reprocesar videos ya importados")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    s = load_settings()\n    ensure_dirs(s["gestures"])\n    clip_s = float(s["sequence"]["clip_seconds"])\n    min_ratio = float(s["dataset"]["min_valid_ratio"])\n    mirror = bool(s["camera"].get("mirror", True))\n    total = 0\n    for g in s["gestures"]:\n        for video in sorted((Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "data" / "raw_videos" / g).glob("*")):\n            if video.suffix.lower() not in VIDEO_EXT:\n                continue\n            done = LANDMARKS / g / f"{video.stem}.done"\n            if done.exists() and not args.force:\n                continue\n            lm, t = extract(video, mirror)\n            if lm is None or t[-1] <= 0:\n                print(f"[{g}] {video.name}: no se pudo leer")\n                continue\n            dur = float(t[-1])\n            starts = [0.0] if dur <= clip_s * 1.6 else list(np.arange(0.0, dur - clip_s * 0.5, clip_s))\n            n = 0\n            for k, a in enumerate(starts):\n                b = dur + 1e-6 if len(starts) == 1 else a + clip_s\n                m = (t >= a) & (t < b)\n                if m.sum() < 5 or valid_mask(lm[m]).mean() < min_ratio:\n                    continue\n                np.savez_compressed(LANDMARKS / g / f"vid_{video.stem}_s{k:02d}.npz",\n                                    lm=lm[m].astype(np.float32), t=t[m] - t[m][0],\n                                    session=np.array(f"vid_{video.stem}"))\n                n += 1\n            done.touch()\n            total += n\n            print(f"[{g}] {video.name}: {n} clip(s) válidos de {len(starts)} segmento(s)")\n    print(f"\\nImportados {total} clips. Siguiente paso: build_dataset.py")\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n',
    'scripts/pipeline.py': '"""Ejecuta en secuencia: importar videos -> construir dataset -> entrenar -> testear.\n\n  python scripts/pipeline.py                   # todo\n  python scripts/pipeline.py --skip-import     # sin importar videos\n"""\nimport argparse\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument("--skip-import", action="store_true")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    steps = ([] if args.skip_import else ["import_videos.py"]) + ["build_dataset.py", "train.py", "test.py"]\n    for s in steps:\n        print(f"\\n===== {s} =====", flush=True)\n        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, "-u", str(ROOT / "scripts" / s)], cwd=ROOT)\n        if r.returncode != 0:\n            raise SystemExit(f"Falló {s} (código {r.returncode}). Pipeline detenido.")\n    print("\\nPipeline completo.")\n',
    'scripts/record.py': '"""Graba clips de gestos con la cámara y guarda sus landmarks (y opcionalmente el video).\n\nTeclas:  1-9 elegir gesto · ESPACIO grabar clip · U deshacer último · V guardar video on/off · Q/ESC salir\n"""\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "src"))\n\nimport cv2  # noqa: E402\nimport numpy as np  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom gesture_control.camera import open_camera  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.config import load_settings  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.dataset import clip_files  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.features import RAW_DIM, valid_mask  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.hands import HandTracker, draw  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.paths import LANDMARKS, RAW_VIDEOS, ensure_dirs  # noqa: E402\n\nWIN = "Grabar gestos"\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument("--save-video", action="store_true", help="guardar también el .mp4 de cada clip")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    s = load_settings()\n    gestures = s["gestures"]\n    ensure_dirs(gestures)\n    clip_s = float(s["sequence"]["clip_seconds"])\n    min_ratio = float(s["dataset"]["min_valid_ratio"])\n    mirror = bool(s["camera"].get("mirror", True))\n    session = datetime.now().strftime("rec%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")\n    save_video = args.save_video\n\n    cap = open_camera(s)\n    tracker = HandTracker()\n    t0 = time.monotonic()\n    zeros = np.zeros(RAW_DIM, np.float32)\n    sel, counter, saved = 0, 0, []\n    msg, msg_until = "", 0.0\n\n    def grab():\n        ok, raw = cap.read()\n        if not ok:\n            return None, None, None\n        disp = cv2.flip(raw, 1) if mirror else raw\n        lm = tracker.process(disp, (time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000)\n        return raw, disp, lm\n\n    def show(disp, lm, header, color=(255, 255, 255), border=None):\n        img = draw(disp.copy(), lm)\n        cv2.putText(img, header, (10, 28), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.75, color, 2)\n        counts = "  ".join(f"{i + 1}:{g[:8]}={len(clip_files(g))}" for i, g in enumerate(gestures))\n        cv2.putText(img, counts, (10, img.shape[0] - 12), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.45, (200, 255, 200), 1)\n        if border:\n            cv2.rectangle(img, (0, 0), (img.shape[1] - 1, img.shape[0] - 1), border, 6)\n        cv2.imshow(WIN, img)\n        return cv2.waitKey(1) & 0xFF\n\n    def record():\n        nonlocal counter, msg, msg_until\n        g = gestures[sel]\n        for n in (3, 2, 1):\n            end = time.monotonic() + 0.6\n            while time.monotonic() < end:\n                _, disp, lm = grab()\n                if disp is not None:\n                    show(disp, lm, f"Prepárate: {g}  ({n})", (0, 255, 255))\n        lms, ts, frames = [], [], []\n        start = time.monotonic()\n        while time.monotonic() - start < clip_s:\n            raw, disp, lm = grab()\n            if disp is None:\n                continue\n            lms.append(lm if lm is not None else zeros)\n            ts.append(time.monotonic() - start)\n            if save_video:\n                frames.append(raw)\n            show(disp, lm, f"GRABANDO: {g}", (0, 0, 255), border=(0, 0, 255))\n        arr, t = np.stack(lms), np.array(ts)\n        ratio = float(valid_mask(arr).mean())\n        if ratio < min_ratio:\n            msg, msg_until = f"Descartado: mano detectada en {ratio:.0%} de los frames", time.time() + 3\n            return\n        counter += 1\n        stem = f"{session}_{counter:03d}"\n        path = LANDMARKS / g / f"{stem}.npz"\n        np.savez_compressed(path, lm=arr.astype(np.float32), t=t, session=np.array(session))\n        saved.append(path)\n        if save_video and frames:\n            fps = len(frames) / max(t[-1], 1e-3)\n            h, w = frames[0].shape[:2]\n            vw = cv2.VideoWriter(str(RAW_VIDEOS / g / f"{stem}.mp4"), cv2.VideoWriter_fourcc(*"mp4v"), fps, (w, h))\n            for fr in frames:\n                vw.write(fr)\n            vw.release()\n            (LANDMARKS / g / f"{stem}.done").touch()  # ya está procesado: no re-importar\n        msg, msg_until = f"Guardado {path.name} ({ratio:.0%} con mano)", time.time() + 2\n\n    print(__doc__)\n    try:\n        while True:\n            _, disp, lm = grab()\n            if disp is None:\n                continue\n            head = f"[{sel + 1}] {gestures[sel]} · ESPACIO grabar · video {\'ON\' if save_video else \'off\'}"\n            key = show(disp, lm, msg if time.time() < msg_until else head)\n            if key in (ord("q"), 27):\n                break\n            if key == 32:\n                record()\n            elif key == ord("v"):\n                save_video = not save_video\n            elif key == ord("u") and saved:\n                p = saved.pop()\n                p.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n                msg, msg_until = f"Eliminado {p.name}", time.time() + 2\n            elif ord("1") <= key <= ord("9") and key - ord("1") < len(gestures):\n                sel = key - ord("1")\n    finally:\n        cap.release()\n        tracker.close()\n        cv2.destroyAllWindows()\n    print(f"Sesión {session}: {len(saved)} clips guardados. Siguiente paso: build_dataset.py")\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n',
    'scripts/run.py': '"""Inicia/detiene el demonio de reconocimiento.\n\n  python scripts/run.py                  # en primer plano\n  python scripts/run.py --dry-run        # solo muestra las acciones, no las ejecuta\n  python scripts/run.py --background     # desacoplado (sigue al cerrar la terminal)\n  python scripts/run.py --status | --stop\n"""\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "src"))\n\nfrom gesture_control.daemon import main  # noqa: E402\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n',
    'scripts/test.py': '"""Evalúa el modelo sobre el set de test (accuracy, reporte, matriz de confusión)."""\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "src"))\n\nfrom gesture_control.config import load_settings  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.evaluation import evaluate  # noqa: E402\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    evaluate(load_settings())\n',
    'scripts/train.py': '"""Entrena el modelo con data/splits (split \'train\', validación con \'val\')."""\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / "src"))\n\nfrom gesture_control.config import load_settings  # noqa: E402\nfrom gesture_control.training import train  # noqa: E402\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    train(load_settings())\n',
    'src/gesture_control/__init__.py': '"""Gesture Control: control de ventanas con gestos de una mano (MediaPipe + TensorFlow)."""\n__version__ = "0.1.0"\n',
    'src/gesture_control/actions.py': '"""Ejecución de acciones de ventana según el sistema operativo (pynput / ydotool / comando)."""\nimport os\nimport shlex\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport time\n\nfrom .config import load_actions\n\nDESTRUCTIVE = {"close_window"}\n\n# Códigos de linux/input-event-codes.h (para ydotool)\nYDO = {\n    "esc": 1, "tab": 15, "enter": 28, "ctrl": 29, "shift": 42, "alt": 56, "space": 57,\n    "meta": 125, "win": 125, "super": 125, "cmd": 125,\n    "up": 103, "left": 105, "right": 106, "down": 108,\n    "f1": 59, "f2": 60, "f3": 61, "f4": 62, "f5": 63, "f6": 64, "f7": 65, "f8": 66,\n    "f9": 67, "f10": 68, "f11": 87, "f12": 88,\n}\nfor _c, _n in zip("qwertyuiop", range(16, 26)):\n    YDO[_c] = _n\nfor _c, _n in zip("asdfghjkl", range(30, 39)):\n    YDO[_c] = _n\nfor _c, _n in zip("zxcvbnm", range(44, 51)):\n    YDO[_c] = _n\n\n\ndef resolve_backend(settings, info):\n    choice = settings.get("system", {}).get("backend", "auto")\n    if choice != "auto":\n        return choice\n    if info["system"] == "linux" and info["wayland"]:\n        return "ydotool" if shutil.which("ydotool") else "pynput"\n    return "pynput"\n\n\nclass PynputBackend:\n    name = "pynput"\n    _alias = {"win": "cmd", "meta": "cmd", "super": "cmd", "control": "ctrl",\n              "escape": "esc", "return": "enter"}\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        from pynput.keyboard import Controller, Key\n        self._kb = Controller()\n        self._Key = Key\n\n    def _k(self, name):\n        n = self._alias.get(name.lower(), name.lower())\n        if len(n) == 1:\n            return n\n        k = getattr(self._Key, n, None)\n        if k is None:\n            raise ValueError(f"Tecla desconocida: {name}")\n        return k\n\n    def press(self, name):\n        self._kb.press(self._k(name))\n        time.sleep(0.02)\n\n    def release(self, name):\n        self._kb.release(self._k(name))\n        time.sleep(0.02)\n\n    def tap(self, name, mods=()):\n        mods = list(mods)\n        for m in mods:\n            self.press(m)\n        self.press(name)\n        self.release(name)\n        for m in reversed(mods):\n            self.release(m)\n\n\nclass YdotoolBackend:\n    name = "ydotool"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        if not shutil.which("ydotool"):\n            raise RuntimeError("ydotool no está instalado (y ydotoold debe estar corriendo).")\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _code(name):\n        c = YDO.get(name.lower())\n        if c is None:\n            raise ValueError(f"Tecla desconocida para ydotool: {name}")\n        return c\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _run(seq):\n        subprocess.run(["ydotool", "key", *seq], check=False,\n                       stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n\n    def press(self, name):\n        self._run([f"{self._code(name)}:1"])\n\n    def release(self, name):\n        self._run([f"{self._code(name)}:0"])\n\n    def tap(self, name, mods=()):\n        m = [self._code(x) for x in mods]\n        c = self._code(name)\n        self._run([f"{x}:1" for x in m] + [f"{c}:1", f"{c}:0"] + [f"{x}:0" for x in reversed(m)])\n\n\nclass ActionRunner:\n    def __init__(self, settings, info):\n        self.info = info\n        self.cfg = load_actions()\n        self.backend_name = resolve_backend(settings, info)\n        self.alt_hold = float(settings["inference"].get("alt_hold_seconds", 1.2))\n        self._backend = None\n        self._alt_active = False\n        self._alt_last = 0.0\n\n    # ---- resolución ----\n    @property\n    def backend(self):\n        if self._backend is None:\n            self._backend = YdotoolBackend() if self.backend_name == "ydotool" else PynputBackend()\n        return self._backend\n\n    def action_for(self, gesture):\n        return (self.cfg.get("gestures") or {}).get(gesture)\n\n    def _spec(self, action):\n        table = (self.cfg.get("actions") or {}).get(action)\n        if not table:\n            return None\n        order = []\n        if self.info["system"] == "linux":\n            if self.info["wayland"]:\n                order.append("linux_wayland")\n            order.append("linux")\n        else:\n            order.append(self.info["system"])\n        order.append("all")\n        for key in order:\n            if key in table:\n                return table[key]\n        return None\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _text(spec):\n        if "alt_tab" in spec:\n            return "Alt+Tab" if spec["alt_tab"] != "backward" else "Alt+Shift+Tab"\n        if "keys" in spec:\n            return spec["keys"]\n        return f"cmd: {spec.get(\'cmd\')}"\n\n    # ---- ejecución ----\n    def run(self, action, dry_run=False):\n        spec = self._spec(action)\n        if spec is None:\n            return f"{action}: sin definición para este sistema"\n        text = f"{action} ({self._text(spec)})"\n        if dry_run:\n            return f"[dry-run] {text}"\n        if "alt_tab" in spec:\n            self._alt_tab(spec["alt_tab"] == "backward")\n        else:\n            self.release_alt()\n            if "keys" in spec:\n                parts = [p.strip() for p in spec["keys"].split("+")]\n                self.backend.tap(parts[-1], parts[:-1])\n            elif "cmd" in spec:\n                subprocess.Popen(shlex.split(spec["cmd"], posix=(os.name != "nt")),\n                                 stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n        return text\n\n    def _alt_tab(self, backward):\n        if not self._alt_active:\n            self.backend.press("alt")\n            self._alt_active = True\n        self.backend.tap("tab", ["shift"] if backward else [])\n        self._alt_last = time.monotonic()\n\n    def tick(self):\n        """Suelta Alt cuando pasó el tiempo de espera sin nuevos swipes."""\n        if self._alt_active and time.monotonic() - self._alt_last > self.alt_hold:\n            self.release_alt()\n\n    def release_alt(self):\n        if self._alt_active:\n            try:\n                self.backend.release("alt")\n            finally:\n                self._alt_active = False\n',
    'src/gesture_control/camera.py': '"""Apertura de cámara (misma lógica en Linux y Windows)."""\nimport os\n\nimport cv2\n\n\ndef open_camera(settings):\n    cam = settings["camera"]\n    idx = int(cam.get("index", 0))\n    if os.name == "nt":\n        cap = cv2.VideoCapture(idx, cv2.CAP_DSHOW)\n    else:\n        cap = cv2.VideoCapture(idx)\n    if not cap.isOpened():\n        raise RuntimeError(f"No se pudo abrir la cámara {idx}. Revisa camera.index en config/settings.yaml.")\n    cap.set(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_WIDTH, int(cam.get("width", 640)))\n    cap.set(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_HEIGHT, int(cam.get("height", 480)))\n    cap.set(cv2.CAP_PROP_BUFFERSIZE, 1)\n    return cap\n',
    'src/gesture_control/config.py': 'import re\n\nimport yaml\n\nfrom .paths import ACTIONS_FILE, SETTINGS_FILE\n\n\ndef _load(path):\n    with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        return yaml.safe_load(f) or {}\n\n\ndef load_settings():\n    return _load(SETTINGS_FILE)\n\n\ndef save_settings(settings):\n    """Reescribe todo el archivo (pierde los comentarios). Preferir update_settings."""\n    with open(SETTINGS_FILE, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        yaml.safe_dump(settings, f, sort_keys=False, allow_unicode=True)\n\n\ndef _fmt(value):\n    if isinstance(value, bool):\n        return "true" if value else "false"\n    return str(value)\n\n\ndef update_settings(changes):\n    """Cambia solo los valores indicados {(seccion, clave): valor} conservando comentarios."""\n    lines = SETTINGS_FILE.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines()\n    pending = dict(changes)\n    section = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        m = re.match(r"^(\\w+):\\s*(#.*)?$", line)\n        if m:\n            section = m.group(1)\n            continue\n        m = re.match(r"^(\\s+)(\\w+):\\s*([^#]*?)(\\s*)(#.*)?$", line)\n        if m and (section, m.group(2)) in pending:\n            val = _fmt(pending.pop((section, m.group(2))))\n            lines[i] = f"{m.group(1)}{m.group(2)}: {val}{m.group(4) or \'\'}{m.group(5) or \'\'}"\n    SETTINGS_FILE.write_text("\\n".join(lines) + "\\n", encoding="utf-8")\n    if pending:  # clave nueva que no estaba en el archivo: respaldo completo\n        s = load_settings()\n        for (a, b), v in pending.items():\n            s.setdefault(a, {})[b] = v\n        save_settings(s)\n\n\ndef load_actions():\n    return _load(ACTIONS_FILE)\n',
    'src/gesture_control/daemon.py': '"""Demonio: mantiene la cámara abierta, reconoce gestos en vivo y ejecuta acciones."""\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport signal\nimport time\nfrom collections import deque\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom . import osinfo, status\nfrom .actions import DESTRUCTIVE, ActionRunner\nfrom .config import load_settings\nfrom .features import FEAT_DIM, RAW_DIM, make_features\nfrom .paths import (COMMAND_FILE, LABELS_FILE, MODEL_FILE, PID_FILE, RUNTIME, STATUS_FILE,\n                    STOP_FLAG, ensure_dirs)\n\n\ndef _write_status(**kw):\n    status.write_json_atomic(STATUS_FILE, {**kw, "ts": time.time()})\n\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Demonio de reconocimiento de gestos")\n    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="detecta y muestra la acción, sin ejecutarla")\n    ap.add_argument("--preview", action="store_true", help="ventana con la cámara y el esqueleto")\n    ap.add_argument("--background", action="store_true", help="lanzar desacoplado y salir")\n    ap.add_argument("--stop", action="store_true", help="detener el demonio en ejecución")\n    ap.add_argument("--status", action="store_true", help="mostrar el estado del demonio")\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n\n    if args.stop:\n        print("Demonio detenido." if status.stop_daemon() else "El demonio no está corriendo.")\n        return\n    if args.status:\n        pid = status.daemon_pid()\n        print(f"Corriendo (pid {pid})\\n{json.dumps(status.read_daemon_status(), indent=1)}" if pid\n              else "Detenido.")\n        return\n    if args.background:\n        if status.daemon_pid():\n            print(f"Ya está corriendo (pid {status.daemon_pid()}).")\n        else:\n            print(f"Demonio lanzado en segundo plano (pid {status.start_daemon(args.dry_run, args.preview)}).")\n        return\n    if status.daemon_pid():\n        raise SystemExit(f"Ya hay un demonio corriendo (pid {status.daemon_pid()}). Usa --stop.")\n\n    os.environ.setdefault("TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL", "2")\n    settings = load_settings()\n    ensure_dirs(settings["gestures"])\n    RUNTIME.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    PID_FILE.write_text(str(os.getpid()))\n    STOP_FLAG.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    dry_run = args.dry_run\n    base = {"pid": os.getpid(), "dry_run": dry_run}\n    _write_status(state="starting", message="cargando modelo", **base)\n\n    stop = {"flag": False}\n    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, lambda *_: stop.update(flag=True))\n    signal.signal(signal.SIGINT, lambda *_: stop.update(flag=True))\n\n    runner = cap = tracker = None\n    try:\n        if not MODEL_FILE.exists():\n            raise RuntimeError("No hay modelo entrenado (models/gesture_model.keras). Ejecuta train.py.")\n        with open(LABELS_FILE, encoding="utf-8") as f:\n            labels = json.load(f)["gestures"]\n        import cv2\n        from tensorflow import keras\n        from .camera import open_camera\n        from .hands import HandTracker, draw\n\n        steps = int(settings["sequence"]["steps"])\n        model = keras.models.load_model(MODEL_FILE)\n        model(np.zeros((1, steps, FEAT_DIM), np.float32), training=False)  # calentamiento\n\n        info = osinfo.detect()\n        runner = ActionRunner(settings, info)\n        tracker = HandTracker()\n        cap = open_camera(settings)\n        inf = settings["inference"]\n        clip_s = float(settings["sequence"]["clip_seconds"])\n        mirror = bool(settings["camera"].get("mirror", True))\n        zeros = np.zeros(RAW_DIM, np.float32)\n\n        buf = deque()\n        t0 = time.monotonic()\n        frame_i = fails = streak = 0\n        streak_label = None\n        cooldown_until = 0.0\n        last = {"last_gesture": None, "last_conf": None, "last_action": None, "last_time": None}\n        fps_t, fps_n, fps = t0, 0, 0.0\n        next_status = cmd_mtime = 0.0\n        hand = False\n        preview = args.preview\n        print(f"Demonio listo · {runner.backend_name} · dry_run={dry_run}", flush=True)\n\n        while not stop["flag"] and not STOP_FLAG.exists():\n            ok, frame = cap.read()\n            if not ok:\n                fails += 1\n                if fails > 100:\n                    raise RuntimeError("La cámara dejó de entregar imágenes.")\n                time.sleep(0.02)\n                continue\n            fails = 0\n            if mirror:\n                frame = cv2.flip(frame, 1)\n            now = time.monotonic() - t0\n            lm = tracker.process(frame, now * 1000)\n            hand = lm is not None\n            buf.append((now, lm if hand else zeros))\n            while buf and now - buf[0][0] > clip_s:\n                buf.popleft()\n            frame_i += 1\n            fps_n += 1\n            runner.tick()\n\n            if (frame_i % int(inf["predict_every"]) == 0 and now >= cooldown_until\n                    and buf[-1][0] - buf[0][0] >= 0.9 * clip_s):\n                arr = np.stack([b[1] for b in buf])\n                ts = np.array([b[0] for b in buf])\n                x = make_features(arr, ts, steps, min_ratio=float(inf["min_hand_ratio"]))\n                label, conf = None, 0.0\n                if x is not None:\n                    probs = model(x[None], training=False).numpy()[0]\n                    k = int(probs.argmax())\n                    label, conf = labels[k], float(probs[k])\n                action = runner.action_for(label) if label else None\n                need = float(inf["destructive_threshold"] if action in DESTRUCTIVE else inf["threshold"])\n                if label and label != "ninguno" and action and conf >= need:\n                    streak = streak + 1 if label == streak_label else 1\n                    streak_label = label\n                    if streak >= int(inf["votes"]) + (1 if action in DESTRUCTIVE else 0):\n                        try:\n                            msg = runner.run(action, dry_run)\n                        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n                            msg = f"ERROR en {action}: {e}"\n                        print(f"[{time.strftime(\'%H:%M:%S\')}] {label} ({conf:.2f}) -> {msg}", flush=True)\n                        last = {"last_gesture": label, "last_conf": round(conf, 3),\n                                "last_action": msg, "last_time": time.strftime("%H:%M:%S")}\n                        cooldown_until = now + float(inf["cooldown"])\n                        buf.clear()\n                        streak, streak_label = 0, None\n                else:\n                    streak, streak_label = 0, None\n\n            tm = time.monotonic()\n            if tm - fps_t >= 1.0:\n                fps, fps_n, fps_t = fps_n / (tm - fps_t), 0, tm\n            if tm >= next_status:\n                next_status = tm + 0.5\n                if COMMAND_FILE.exists() and COMMAND_FILE.stat().st_mtime != cmd_mtime:\n                    cmd_mtime = COMMAND_FILE.stat().st_mtime\n                    cmd = status.read_json(COMMAND_FILE) or {}\n                    if "dry_run" in cmd:\n                        dry_run = bool(cmd["dry_run"])\n                _write_status(state="running", pid=os.getpid(), dry_run=dry_run, fps=round(fps, 1),\n                              hand=hand, backend=runner.backend_name, **last)\n            if preview:\n                try:\n                    draw(frame, lm)\n                    cv2.putText(frame, f"{\'DRY-RUN \' if dry_run else \'\'}{last[\'last_gesture\'] or \'-\'}",\n                                (10, 25), cv2.FONT_HERSHEY_SIMPLEX, 0.7, (255, 255, 255), 2)\n                    cv2.imshow("Gesture Control", frame)\n                    if cv2.waitKey(1) & 0xFF in (ord("q"), 27):\n                        break\n                except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n                    preview = False\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        print(f"ERROR: {e}", flush=True)\n        _write_status(state="error", message=str(e), **base)\n        raise\n    finally:\n        if runner:\n            try:\n                runner.release_alt()\n            except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n                pass\n        if cap:\n            cap.release()\n        if tracker:\n            tracker.close()\n        PID_FILE.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n        STOP_FLAG.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n        if not (status.read_json(STATUS_FILE) or {}).get("state") == "error":\n            _write_status(state="stopped", **base)\n        print("Demonio detenido.", flush=True)\n',
    'src/gesture_control/dataset.py': '"""Splits train/val/test y carga de datos (solo numpy, sin TensorFlow)."""\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport time\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom .features import FEAT_DIM, make_features\nfrom .paths import LANDMARKS, SPLITS, SPLITS_FILE\n\n\ndef clip_files(gesture):\n    d = LANDMARKS / gesture\n    return sorted(d.glob("*.npz")) if d.exists() else []\n\n\ndef _session_of(path):\n    with np.load(path) as d:\n        return str(d["session"])\n\n\ndef build_splits(settings):\n    """Divide por sesión de grabación (o por bloques cronológicos si hay pocas sesiones)."""\n    ds = settings["dataset"]\n    rng = random.Random(ds.get("seed", 42))\n    val_r, test_r = ds["val_ratio"], ds["test_ratio"]\n    files_map, report = {}, {}\n    for g in settings["gestures"]:\n        files = clip_files(g)\n        n = len(files)\n        if n == 0:\n            report[g] = {"clips": 0, "mode": "-", "train": 0, "val": 0, "test": 0}\n            continue\n        by_sess = defaultdict(list)\n        for f in files:\n            by_sess[_session_of(f)].append(f)\n        if len(by_sess) >= 3:\n            mode = f"sesiones ({len(by_sess)})"\n            sess = list(by_sess.values())\n            rng.shuffle(sess)\n            t_target, v_target = max(1, math.ceil(n * test_r)), max(1, math.ceil(n * val_r))\n            train, val, test = [], [], []\n            remaining = len(sess)\n            for fs in sess:\n                if len(test) < t_target and remaining > 2:\n                    test += fs\n                elif len(val) < v_target and remaining > 1:\n                    val += fs\n                else:\n                    train += fs\n                remaining -= 1\n        else:\n            mode = "bloques cronológicos"\n            if n < 5:\n                train, val, test = files, [], []\n            else:\n                n_test, n_val = max(1, round(n * test_r)), max(1, round(n * val_r))\n                train = files[: n - n_val - n_test]\n                val = files[n - n_val - n_test: n - n_test]\n                test = files[n - n_test:]\n        for sp, group in (("train", train), ("val", val), ("test", test)):\n            for f in group:\n                files_map[f"{g}/{f.name}"] = sp\n        report[g] = {"clips": n, "mode": mode, "train": len(train), "val": len(val), "test": len(test)}\n    SPLITS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(SPLITS_FILE, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        json.dump({"built": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), "files": files_map}, f, indent=1)\n    return report\n\n\ndef load_splits():\n    if not SPLITS_FILE.exists():\n        return {}\n    try:\n        with open(SPLITS_FILE, encoding="utf-8") as f:\n            return json.load(f).get("files", {})\n    except (OSError, ValueError):\n        return {}\n\n\ndef load_xy(settings, split, augment=False, seed=0):\n    idx = {g: i for i, g in enumerate(settings["gestures"])}\n    steps = settings["sequence"]["steps"]\n    min_ratio = settings["dataset"]["min_valid_ratio"]\n    k_aug = int(settings["training"]["aug_factor"]) if augment else 0\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    X, y = [], []\n    for key, sp in load_splits().items():\n        g = key.split("/")[0]\n        path = LANDMARKS / key\n        if sp != split or g not in idx or not path.exists():\n            continue\n        with np.load(path) as d:\n            lm, t = d["lm"], d["t"]\n        for k in range(1 + k_aug):\n            x = make_features(lm, t, steps, augment=k > 0, rng=rng, min_ratio=min_ratio)\n            if x is not None:\n                X.append(x)\n                y.append(idx[g])\n    if not X:\n        return np.zeros((0, steps, FEAT_DIM), np.float32), np.zeros((0,), np.int64)\n    return np.stack(X).astype(np.float32), np.array(y, dtype=np.int64)\n',
    'src/gesture_control/evaluation.py': '"""Evaluación sobre el set de test: accuracy, reporte por clase y matriz de confusión."""\nimport json\nimport os\n\nfrom .dataset import load_xy\nfrom .paths import CONFUSION_PNG, LABELS_FILE, MODEL_FILE, TEST_RESULTS_FILE\n\n\ndef evaluate(settings):\n    os.environ.setdefault("TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL", "2")\n    from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix\n    from tensorflow import keras\n\n    if not MODEL_FILE.exists():\n        raise SystemExit("No hay modelo entrenado. Ejecuta train.py primero.")\n    with open(LABELS_FILE, encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        gestures = json.load(f)["gestures"]\n    X, y = load_xy(settings, "test", augment=False)\n    if len(X) == 0:\n        raise SystemExit("El set de test está vacío. Graba más clips y ejecuta build_dataset.py.")\n    model = keras.models.load_model(MODEL_FILE)\n    pred = model.predict(X, verbose=0).argmax(axis=1)\n    labels = list(range(len(gestures)))\n    acc = float((pred == y).mean())\n    cm = confusion_matrix(y, pred, labels=labels)\n    rep = classification_report(y, pred, labels=labels, target_names=gestures,\n                                zero_division=0, output_dict=True)\n    print(f"Test: {len(X)} clips · accuracy {acc:.1%}\\n")\n    print(classification_report(y, pred, labels=labels, target_names=gestures, zero_division=0))\n    print("Matriz de confusión (filas = real, columnas = predicho):")\n    print(cm)\n    with open(TEST_RESULTS_FILE, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        json.dump({"accuracy": acc, "n_test": int(len(X)), "labels": gestures,\n                   "confusion": cm.tolist(), "per_class": rep}, f, indent=1)\n    _plot(cm, gestures, acc)\n\n\ndef _plot(cm, labels, acc):\n    import matplotlib\n    matplotlib.use("Agg")\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 5))\n    ax.imshow(cm, cmap="Blues")\n    ax.set_xticks(range(len(labels)), labels, rotation=45, ha="right")\n    ax.set_yticks(range(len(labels)), labels)\n    for i in range(len(labels)):\n        for j in range(len(labels)):\n            ax.text(j, i, str(cm[i, j]), ha="center", va="center",\n                    color="white" if cm[i, j] > cm.max() / 2 else "black")\n    ax.set_xlabel("Predicho")\n    ax.set_ylabel("Real")\n    ax.set_title(f"Matriz de confusión · accuracy {acc:.1%}")\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(CONFUSION_PNG, dpi=120)\n    plt.close(fig)\n',
    'src/gesture_control/features.py': '"""Preprocesado de secuencias de landmarks (solo numpy, sin TensorFlow)."""\nimport numpy as np\n\nN_POINTS = 21\nRAW_DIM = N_POINTS * 3          # 63 valores por frame\nFEAT_DIM = RAW_DIM + 3          # + trayectoria de la muñeca\n\n\ndef valid_mask(lm):\n    """Frames donde se detectó la mano (los frames sin mano se guardan en ceros)."""\n    return np.abs(lm).sum(axis=1) > 0\n\n\ndef resample(lm, t, steps):\n    """(T,63) con tiempos t -> (steps,63) en una malla uniforme. Devuelve (seq|None, ratio_válidos)."""\n    lm = np.asarray(lm, dtype=np.float64)\n    t = np.asarray(t, dtype=np.float64)\n    if len(t) == 0:\n        return None, 0.0\n    valid = valid_mask(lm)\n    ratio = float(valid.mean())\n    if valid.sum() < 2 or t[-1] <= t[0]:\n        return None, ratio\n    grid = np.linspace(t[0], t[-1], steps)\n    tv = t[valid]\n    out = np.empty((steps, lm.shape[1]))\n    for j in range(lm.shape[1]):\n        out[:, j] = np.interp(grid, tv, lm[valid, j])\n    return out, ratio\n\n\ndef normalize(seq):\n    """Forma de la mano relativa a la muñeca + trayectoria de la muñeca, ambas en unidades de palma."""\n    s = seq.shape[0]\n    p = seq.reshape(s, N_POINTS, 3)\n    wrist = p[:, 0, :]\n    scale = float(np.median(np.linalg.norm(p[:, 9, :2] - p[:, 0, :2], axis=1)))\n    scale = max(scale, 0.02)\n    shape = (p - wrist[:, None, :]) / scale\n    traj = (wrist - wrist[0]) / scale\n    return np.concatenate([shape.reshape(s, RAW_DIM), traj], axis=1).astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef _crop_time(lm, t, rng):\n    span = t[-1] - t[0]\n    a = t[0] + rng.uniform(0, 0.15) * span\n    b = t[-1] - rng.uniform(0, 0.15) * span\n    keep = (t >= a) & (t <= b)\n    if keep.sum() < 4:\n        return lm, t\n    return lm[keep], t[keep]\n\n\ndef _augment_seq(seq, rng):\n    p = seq.reshape(-1, N_POINTS, 3).copy()\n    origin = p[0, 0, :2].copy()\n    ang = np.deg2rad(rng.uniform(-10, 10))\n    c, s = np.cos(ang), np.sin(ang)\n    rot = np.array([[c, -s], [s, c]])\n    xy = (p[:, :, :2] - origin) @ rot.T\n    xy *= rng.uniform(0.92, 1.08, size=2)\n    p[:, :, :2] = xy + origin\n    p += rng.normal(0, 0.004, p.shape)\n    return p.reshape(seq.shape)\n\n\ndef make_features(lm, t, steps, augment=False, rng=None, min_ratio=0.0):\n    """Clip crudo -> matriz (steps, FEAT_DIM) o None si el clip no sirve."""\n    lm = np.asarray(lm, dtype=np.float64)\n    t = np.asarray(t, dtype=np.float64)\n    if augment:\n        rng = rng or np.random.default_rng()\n        lm, t = _crop_time(lm, t, rng)\n    seq, ratio = resample(lm, t, steps)\n    if seq is None or ratio < min_ratio:\n        return None\n    if augment:\n        seq = _augment_seq(seq, rng)\n    return normalize(seq)\n',
    'src/gesture_control/gui.py': '"""Panel de control (Tkinter + Matplotlib). Cerrar la ventana NO detiene el demonio."""\nimport queue\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport tkinter as tk\nfrom tkinter import messagebox, ttk\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport yaml\nfrom matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import FigureCanvasTkAgg\nfrom matplotlib.figure import Figure\n\nfrom . import osinfo, status\nfrom .actions import resolve_backend\nfrom .config import load_settings, update_settings\nfrom .paths import ACTIONS_FILE, HISTORY_FILE, ROOT, SCRIPTS, TEST_RESULTS_FILE, ensure_dirs\n\nGREEN, RED, AMBER = "#1e8e3e", "#c5221f", "#b06000"\n\n\nclass App(tk.Tk):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.title("Gesture Control")\n        self.geometry("1020x780")\n        self.minsize(900, 680)\n        self.settings = load_settings()\n        ensure_dirs(self.settings["gestures"])\n        self.info = osinfo.detect()\n        self.backend = resolve_backend(self.settings, self.info)\n        self.cam = None\n        self.proc = None\n        self.q = queue.Queue()\n        self.task_buttons = []\n        self.dry = tk.BooleanVar(value=True)\n        self.preview = tk.BooleanVar(value=False)\n        self._build()\n        self.protocol("WM_DELETE_WINDOW", self.on_close)\n        self.check_camera()\n        self.refresh()\n        self.after(100, self.pump)\n        self.after(1000, self.tick)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------ UI\n    def _build(self):\n        nb = ttk.Notebook(self)\n        nb.pack(fill="both", expand=True)\n        home, plots, cfg, acts = (ttk.Frame(nb, padding=8) for _ in range(4))\n        nb.add(home, text="Inicio")\n        nb.add(plots, text="Gráficas")\n        nb.add(cfg, text="Configuración")\n        nb.add(acts, text="Acciones")\n        self._build_home(home)\n        self._build_plots(plots)\n        self._build_cfg(cfg)\n        self._build_actions(acts)\n\n    def _build_home(self, f):\n        self.banner = tk.Label(f, text="…", font=("TkDefaultFont", 18, "bold"), fg="white", pady=8)\n        self.banner.pack(fill="x")\n        ttk.Label(f, text=osinfo.describe(self.info, self.backend)).pack(anchor="w", pady=(6, 4))\n\n        self.checks = ttk.Treeview(f, columns=("ok", "item", "detail"), show="headings", height=6)\n        for c, t, w in (("ok", "", 40), ("item", "Elemento", 170), ("detail", "Detalle", 700)):\n            self.checks.heading(c, text=t)\n            self.checks.column(c, width=w, anchor="w" if c != "ok" else "center")\n        self.checks.pack(fill="x")\n\n        self.table = ttk.Treeview(\n            f, columns=("g", "clips", "train", "val", "test", "vid", "st"), show="headings", height=6)\n        for c, t, w in (("g", "Gesto", 160), ("clips", "Clips", 70), ("train", "Train", 70),\n                        ("val", "Val", 70), ("test", "Test", 70), ("vid", "Videos pend.", 100),\n                        ("st", "Estado", 380)):\n            self.table.heading(c, text=t)\n            self.table.column(c, width=w, anchor="w" if c in ("g", "st") else "center")\n        self.table.pack(fill="x", pady=(8, 0))\n        for t in (self.checks, self.table):\n            t.tag_configure("ok", foreground=GREEN)\n            t.tag_configure("bad", foreground=RED)\n            t.tag_configure("warn", foreground=AMBER)\n\n        row = ttk.LabelFrame(f, text="Datos y modelo", padding=6)\n        row.pack(fill="x", pady=(8, 0))\n        for txt, cmd in (("1 · Grabar datos", lambda: self.task("record.py", ask_stop=True)),\n                         ("2 · Importar videos", lambda: self.task("import_videos.py")),\n                         ("3 · Construir dataset", lambda: self.task("build_dataset.py")),\n                         ("4 · Entrenar", lambda: self.task("train.py")),\n                         ("5 · Testear", lambda: self.task("test.py")),\n                         ("Pipeline 2→5", lambda: self.task("pipeline.py"))):\n            b = ttk.Button(row, text=txt, command=cmd)\n            b.pack(side="left", padx=3)\n            self.task_buttons.append(b)\n        ttk.Button(row, text="↻ Refrescar", command=self.manual_refresh).pack(side="right")\n\n        d = ttk.LabelFrame(f, text="Demonio (fondo, como un live wallpaper)", padding=6)\n        d.pack(fill="x", pady=(8, 0))\n        self.btn_start = ttk.Button(d, text="▶ Iniciar demonio", command=self.start)\n        self.btn_stop = ttk.Button(d, text="■ Detener demonio", command=self.stop)\n        self.btn_start.pack(side="left", padx=3)\n        self.btn_stop.pack(side="left", padx=3)\n        ttk.Checkbutton(d, text="Dry-run (no ejecuta acciones)", variable=self.dry,\n                        command=self.on_dry).pack(side="left", padx=12)\n        ttk.Checkbutton(d, text="Ventana de cámara", variable=self.preview).pack(side="left")\n        self.daemon_lbl = ttk.Label(f, text="", font=("TkDefaultFont", 10, "bold"))\n        self.daemon_lbl.pack(anchor="w", pady=(6, 0))\n\n        lf = ttk.Frame(f)\n        lf.pack(fill="both", expand=True, pady=(6, 0))\n        self.log = tk.Text(lf, height=8, wrap="word", state="disabled", font=("TkFixedFont", 9))\n        sb = ttk.Scrollbar(lf, command=self.log.yview)\n        self.log.configure(yscrollcommand=sb.set)\n        self.log.pack(side="left", fill="both", expand=True)\n        sb.pack(side="right", fill="y")\n\n    def _build_plots(self, f):\n        self.fig = Figure(figsize=(10, 4), dpi=100)\n        self.canvas = FigureCanvasTkAgg(self.fig, master=f)\n        self.canvas.get_tk_widget().pack(fill="both", expand=True)\n\n    def _build_cfg(self, f):\n        s = self.settings\n        spec = [\n            ("Cámara (índice)", ("camera", "index"), int), ("Espejo (true/false)", ("camera", "mirror"), bool),\n            ("Backend (auto/pynput/ydotool)", ("system", "backend"), str),\n            ("Umbral de confianza", ("inference", "threshold"), float),\n            ("Umbral cerrar ventana", ("inference", "destructive_threshold"), float),\n            ("Votos consecutivos", ("inference", "votes"), int),\n            ("Cooldown (s)", ("inference", "cooldown"), float),\n            ("Mantener Alt (s)", ("inference", "alt_hold_seconds"), float),\n            ("Clips mínimos por gesto", ("dataset", "min_clips_per_gesture"), int),\n            ("Épocas", ("training", "epochs"), int),\n            ("Duración del clip (s) *", ("sequence", "clip_seconds"), float),\n        ]\n        self.cfg_vars = []\n        for i, (label, path, typ) in enumerate(spec):\n            ttk.Label(f, text=label).grid(row=i, column=0, sticky="w", pady=2, padx=(0, 12))\n            v = tk.StringVar(value=str(s[path[0]][path[1]]))\n            ttk.Entry(f, textvariable=v, width=18).grid(row=i, column=1, sticky="w")\n            self.cfg_vars.append((path, typ, v))\n        ttk.Button(f, text="Guardar", command=self.save_cfg).grid(row=len(spec), column=0, pady=12, sticky="w")\n        ttk.Label(f, foreground=AMBER, wraplength=700, justify="left",\n                  text="* Cambiar la duración del clip exige volver a grabar/importar y reentrenar. "\n                       "Los cambios aplican al reiniciar el demonio.").grid(\n            row=len(spec) + 1, column=0, columnspan=3, sticky="w")\n\n    def _build_actions(self, f):\n        ttk.Label(f, text="config/actions.yaml: gesto → acción y comandos por sistema").pack(anchor="w")\n        self.actions_txt = tk.Text(f, wrap="none", font=("TkFixedFont", 10))\n        self.actions_txt.pack(fill="both", expand=True, pady=6)\n        self.actions_txt.insert("1.0", ACTIONS_FILE.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))\n        ttk.Button(f, text="Guardar acciones", command=self.save_actions).pack(anchor="w")\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------ estado\n    def check_camera(self):\n        self.cam = (False, "verificando…")\n        threading.Thread(target=lambda: setattr(self, "cam", status.camera_check(self.settings)),\n                         daemon=True).start()\n\n    def manual_refresh(self):\n        self.settings = load_settings()\n        self.check_camera()\n        self.after(1200, self.refresh)\n        self.refresh()\n\n    def refresh(self):\n        checks, ready = status.readiness(self.settings, self.cam)\n        self.checks.delete(*self.checks.get_children())\n        for name, ok, detail, req in checks:\n            tag = "ok" if ok else ("bad" if req else "warn")\n            self.checks.insert("", "end", values=("✔" if ok else "✖", name, detail), tags=(tag,))\n        minc = self.settings["dataset"]["min_clips_per_gesture"]\n        self.table.delete(*self.table.get_children())\n        for r in status.dataset_status(self.settings):\n            problems = []\n            if r["clips"] < minc:\n                problems.append(f"faltan {minc - r[\'clips\']} clips")\n            if r["unsplit"]:\n                problems.append("reconstruir dataset")\n            elif r["clips"] and min(r["train"], r["val"], r["test"]) < 1:\n                problems.append("falta train/val/test")\n            self.table.insert("", "end", tags=("bad" if problems else "ok",), values=(\n                r["gesture"], r["clips"], r["train"], r["val"], r["test"], r["pending_videos"],\n                "✖ " + ", ".join(problems) if problems else "✔ listo"))\n        if ready:\n            self.banner.config(text="LISTO", bg=GREEN)\n        else:\n            falta = [n for n, ok, _, req in checks if req and not ok]\n            self.banner.config(text="FALTA: " + ", ".join(falta), bg=RED)\n        self.update_daemon()\n        self.draw_plots()\n\n    def update_daemon(self):\n        st = status.read_daemon_status()\n        running = st is not None\n        self.btn_start.state(["disabled"] if running else ["!disabled"])\n        self.btn_stop.state(["!disabled"] if running else ["disabled"])\n        if not running:\n            self.daemon_lbl.config(text="Demonio: detenido", foreground="gray")\n            return\n        txt = f"Demonio: {st.get(\'state\')} (pid {st.get(\'pid\')})"\n        if st.get("state") == "running":\n            txt += (f" · {\'DRY-RUN\' if st.get(\'dry_run\') else \'ACCIONES REALES\'} · {st.get(\'fps\', 0)} fps"\n                    f" · mano: {\'sí\' if st.get(\'hand\') else \'no\'}")\n            if st.get("last_gesture"):\n                txt += f" · último: {st[\'last_gesture\']} ({st[\'last_conf\']}) → {st[\'last_action\']}"\n        self.daemon_lbl.config(text=txt, foreground=GREEN)\n\n    def tick(self):\n        self.update_daemon()\n        if not hasattr(self, "_n"):\n            self._n = 0\n        self._n += 1\n        if self._n % 3 == 0 and not self.proc:\n            self.refresh()\n        self.after(1000, self.tick)\n\n    def draw_plots(self):\n        hist, res = status.read_json(HISTORY_FILE), status.read_json(TEST_RESULTS_FILE)\n        fig = self.fig\n        fig.clear()\n        ax1, ax2, ax3 = fig.subplots(1, 3)\n        for ax, keys, title in ((ax1, ("loss", "val_loss"), "Pérdida"),\n                                (ax2, ("accuracy", "val_accuracy"), "Exactitud")):\n            if hist:\n                for k, lab in zip(keys, ("train", "val")):\n                    ax.plot(hist.get(k, []), label=lab)\n                ax.legend()\n                ax.set_xlabel("época")\n            else:\n                ax.text(0.5, 0.5, "sin entrenamiento", ha="center", va="center")\n                ax.set_axis_off()\n            ax.set_title(title)\n        if res:\n            cm, labs = np.array(res["confusion"]), res["labels"]\n            ax3.imshow(cm, cmap="Blues")\n            ax3.set_xticks(range(len(labs)), labs, rotation=60, ha="right", fontsize=7)\n            ax3.set_yticks(range(len(labs)), labs, fontsize=7)\n            for i in range(len(labs)):\n                for j in range(len(labs)):\n                    ax3.text(j, i, cm[i, j], ha="center", va="center", fontsize=8,\n                             color="white" if cm[i, j] > cm.max() / 2 else "black")\n            ax3.set_title(f"Test · {res[\'accuracy\']:.1%}")\n        else:\n            ax3.text(0.5, 0.5, "sin test", ha="center", va="center")\n            ax3.set_axis_off()\n        fig.tight_layout()\n        self.canvas.draw_idle()\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------ tareas\n    def logw(self, text):\n        self.log.config(state="normal")\n        self.log.insert("end", text)\n        self.log.see("end")\n        self.log.config(state="disabled")\n\n    def set_busy(self, busy):\n        for b in self.task_buttons:\n            b.state(["disabled"] if busy else ["!disabled"])\n\n    def task(self, script, ask_stop=False):\n        if self.proc and self.proc.poll() is None:\n            messagebox.showinfo("Ocupado", "Ya hay una tarea en ejecución.")\n            return\n        if ask_stop and status.daemon_pid():\n            if not messagebox.askyesno("Cámara en uso",\n                                       "El demonio está usando la cámara. ¿Detenerlo para grabar?"):\n                return\n            status.stop_daemon()\n        cmd = [sys.executable, "-u", str(SCRIPTS / script)]\n        self.logw(f"\\n$ python scripts/{script}\\n")\n        self.proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, cwd=str(ROOT), stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,\n                                     text=True, bufsize=1, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")\n        self.set_busy(True)\n        threading.Thread(target=self._reader, args=(self.proc,), daemon=True).start()\n\n    def _reader(self, proc):\n        for line in proc.stdout:\n            self.q.put(("line", line))\n        self.q.put(("done", proc.wait()))\n\n    def pump(self):\n        try:\n            while True:\n                kind, val = self.q.get_nowait()\n                if kind == "line":\n                    self.logw(val)\n                else:\n                    self.logw(f"[terminó con código {val}]\\n")\n                    self.proc = None\n                    self.set_busy(False)\n                    self.refresh()\n        except queue.Empty:\n            pass\n        self.after(100, self.pump)\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------ demonio\n    def start(self):\n        checks, _ = status.readiness(self.settings, self.cam)\n        if not next(ok for n, ok, _, _ in checks if n == "Modelo"):\n            messagebox.showerror("Falta el modelo", "Entrena el modelo antes de iniciar el demonio.")\n            return\n        if self.proc and self.proc.poll() is None:\n            messagebox.showinfo("Cámara en uso", "Espera a que termine la tarea actual.")\n            return\n        pid = status.start_daemon(self.dry.get(), self.preview.get())\n        self.logw(f"Demonio lanzado (pid {pid}). Puedes cerrar esta ventana: sigue en segundo plano.\\n")\n        self.after(1500, self.update_daemon)\n\n    def stop(self):\n        status.stop_daemon()\n        self.logw("Demonio detenido.\\n")\n        self.update_daemon()\n\n    def on_dry(self):\n        if status.daemon_pid():\n            status.write_command(dry_run=self.dry.get())\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------ config\n    def save_cfg(self):\n        changes = {}\n        try:\n            for path, typ, var in self.cfg_vars:\n                raw = var.get().strip()\n                changes[path] = (raw.lower() in ("1", "true", "sí", "si", "yes")) if typ is bool else typ(raw)\n        except ValueError as e:\n            messagebox.showerror("Valor inválido", str(e))\n            return\n        update_settings(changes)\n        s = load_settings()\n        self.settings = s\n        self.backend = resolve_backend(s, self.info)\n        self.refresh()\n        messagebox.showinfo("Guardado", "Configuración guardada. Reinicia el demonio para aplicarla.")\n\n    def save_actions(self):\n        text = self.actions_txt.get("1.0", "end")\n        try:\n            yaml.safe_load(text)\n        except yaml.YAMLError as e:\n            messagebox.showerror("YAML inválido", str(e))\n            return\n        ACTIONS_FILE.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")\n        messagebox.showinfo("Guardado", "Acciones guardadas. Reinicia el demonio para aplicarlas.")\n\n    def on_close(self):\n        if self.proc and self.proc.poll() is None:\n            if not messagebox.askyesno("Tarea en curso", "Hay una tarea ejecutándose. ¿Cerrar y cancelarla?"):\n                return\n            self.proc.terminate()\n        if status.daemon_pid():\n            messagebox.showinfo("Demonio activo", "El demonio sigue corriendo en segundo plano.\\n"\n                                "Vuelve a abrir el panel para detenerlo.")\n        self.destroy()\n\n\ndef main():\n    App().mainloop()\n',
    'src/gesture_control/hands.py': '"""Detección de landmarks de una mano con MediaPipe Tasks (HandLandmarker).\n\nUsa solo la API Tasks: `mediapipe.solutions` fue eliminada en versiones recientes.\nEl modelo (.task) se descarga una vez a models/hand_landmarker.task.\n"""\nimport urllib.request\n\nimport cv2\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom .paths import HAND_MODEL_FILE, MODELS\n\nMODEL_URL = (\n    "https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/hand_landmarker/"\n    "hand_landmarker/float16/1/hand_landmarker.task"\n)\n\nCONNECTIONS = [\n    (0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4), (0, 5), (5, 6), (6, 7), (7, 8),\n    (5, 9), (9, 10), (10, 11), (11, 12), (9, 13), (13, 14), (14, 15), (15, 16),\n    (13, 17), (17, 18), (18, 19), (19, 20), (0, 17),\n]\n\n\ndef ensure_hand_model():\n    if HAND_MODEL_FILE.exists() and HAND_MODEL_FILE.stat().st_size > 1000:\n        return HAND_MODEL_FILE\n    MODELS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    print(f"Descargando modelo de manos a {HAND_MODEL_FILE} ...", flush=True)\n    try:\n        tmp = HAND_MODEL_FILE.with_suffix(".tmp")\n        urllib.request.urlretrieve(MODEL_URL, tmp)\n        tmp.replace(HAND_MODEL_FILE)\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            f"No se pudo descargar el modelo de manos ({e}). Descárgalo manualmente de\\n{MODEL_URL}\\n"\n            f"y guárdalo como {HAND_MODEL_FILE}"\n        ) from e\n    return HAND_MODEL_FILE\n\n\nclass HandTracker:\n    def __init__(self, min_detection=0.6, min_tracking=0.5):\n        import mediapipe as mp\n        from mediapipe.tasks import python as mp_python\n        from mediapipe.tasks.python import vision\n\n        self._mp = mp\n        opts = vision.HandLandmarkerOptions(\n            base_options=mp_python.BaseOptions(model_asset_path=str(ensure_hand_model())),\n            running_mode=vision.RunningMode.VIDEO,\n            num_hands=1,\n            min_hand_detection_confidence=min_detection,\n            min_hand_presence_confidence=min_detection,\n            min_tracking_confidence=min_tracking,\n        )\n        self._lm = vision.HandLandmarker.create_from_options(opts)\n        self._last_ts = -1\n\n    def process(self, frame_bgr, ts_ms):\n        """Devuelve un vector (63,) con x,y,z de los 21 puntos, o None si no hay mano."""\n        ts = max(int(ts_ms), self._last_ts + 1)\n        self._last_ts = ts\n        rgb = np.ascontiguousarray(cv2.cvtColor(frame_bgr, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n        image = self._mp.Image(image_format=self._mp.ImageFormat.SRGB, data=rgb)\n        res = self._lm.detect_for_video(image, ts)\n        if not res.hand_landmarks:\n            return None\n        pts = res.hand_landmarks[0]\n        return np.array([[p.x, p.y, p.z] for p in pts], dtype=np.float32).reshape(-1)\n\n    def close(self):\n        try:\n            self._lm.close()\n        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n            pass\n\n\ndef draw(frame, lm, color=(0, 255, 120)):\n    """Dibuja el esqueleto de la mano sobre el frame."""\n    if lm is None:\n        return frame\n    h, w = frame.shape[:2]\n    pts = [(int(x * w), int(y * h)) for x, y in lm.reshape(21, 3)[:, :2]]\n    for a, b in CONNECTIONS:\n        cv2.line(frame, pts[a], pts[b], color, 2)\n    for p in pts:\n        cv2.circle(frame, p, 3, (0, 0, 255), -1)\n    return frame\n',
    'src/gesture_control/model.py': '"""Arquitectura del clasificador de secuencias (TensorFlow/Keras)."""\n\n\ndef build_model(steps, feat_dim, n_classes):\n    from tensorflow import keras\n    from tensorflow.keras import layers\n\n    inp = keras.Input(shape=(steps, feat_dim))\n    x = layers.Conv1D(64, 5, padding="same", activation="relu")(inp)\n    x = layers.BatchNormalization()(x)\n    x = layers.Dropout(0.2)(x)\n    x = layers.Conv1D(64, 3, padding="same", activation="relu")(x)\n    x = layers.BatchNormalization()(x)\n    x = layers.GRU(64)(x)\n    x = layers.Dense(64, activation="relu")(x)\n    x = layers.Dropout(0.3)(x)\n    out = layers.Dense(n_classes, activation="softmax")(x)\n    model = keras.Model(inp, out, name="gesture_gru")\n    model.compile(optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-3),\n                  loss="sparse_categorical_crossentropy", metrics=["accuracy"])\n    return model\n',
    'src/gesture_control/osinfo.py': '"""Detección del sistema operativo y del tipo de sesión gráfica."""\nimport os\nimport platform\n\nNAMES = {"linux": "Linux", "windows": "Windows", "darwin": "macOS"}\n\n\ndef detect():\n    system = platform.system().lower()\n    wayland = system == "linux" and (\n        os.environ.get("XDG_SESSION_TYPE", "").lower() == "wayland"\n        or bool(os.environ.get("WAYLAND_DISPLAY"))\n    )\n    return {\n        "system": system,\n        "wayland": wayland,\n        "desktop": os.environ.get("XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP", ""),\n        "python": platform.python_version(),\n    }\n\n\ndef describe(info, backend):\n    name = NAMES.get(info["system"], info["system"])\n    extra = ""\n    if info["system"] == "linux":\n        extra = " (Wayland)" if info["wayland"] else " (X11)"\n        if info["desktop"]:\n            extra += f" · {info[\'desktop\']}"\n    text = f"{name}{extra} · Python {info[\'python\']} · backend de acciones: {backend}"\n    if info["system"] == "linux" and info["wayland"] and backend == "pynput":\n        text += "\\n⚠ Wayland: pynput no puede enviar teclas. Instala ydotool (ver README) o inicia sesión en X11."\n    return text\n',
    'src/gesture_control/paths.py': '"""Rutas del proyecto. Todo se calcula desde la raíz (la carpeta que contiene src/)."""\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n\nCONFIG_DIR = ROOT / "config"\nSETTINGS_FILE = CONFIG_DIR / "settings.yaml"\nACTIONS_FILE = CONFIG_DIR / "actions.yaml"\n\nDATA_DIR = ROOT / "data"\nRAW_VIDEOS = DATA_DIR / "raw_videos"\nLANDMARKS = DATA_DIR / "landmarks"\nSPLITS = DATA_DIR / "splits"\nSPLITS_FILE = SPLITS / "splits.json"\n\nMODELS = ROOT / "models"\nMODEL_FILE = MODELS / "gesture_model.keras"\nLABELS_FILE = MODELS / "labels.json"\nHISTORY_FILE = MODELS / "history.json"\nTEST_RESULTS_FILE = MODELS / "test_results.json"\nCONFUSION_PNG = MODELS / "confusion_matrix.png"\nHAND_MODEL_FILE = MODELS / "hand_landmarker.task"\n\nRUNTIME = ROOT / "runtime"\nPID_FILE = RUNTIME / "daemon.pid"\nSTATUS_FILE = RUNTIME / "status.json"\nCOMMAND_FILE = RUNTIME / "command.json"\nSTOP_FLAG = RUNTIME / "stop.flag"\nLOG_FILE = RUNTIME / "daemon.log"\n\nSCRIPTS = ROOT / "scripts"\n\n\ndef ensure_dirs(gestures=()):\n    for d in (RAW_VIDEOS, LANDMARKS, SPLITS, MODELS, RUNTIME):\n        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for g in gestures:\n        (RAW_VIDEOS / g).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        (LANDMARKS / g).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef rel(path):\n    """Ruta relativa a la raíz, con \'/\' (portable entre Linux y Windows)."""\n    return Path(path).resolve().relative_to(ROOT).as_posix()\n',
    'src/gesture_control/status.py': '"""Estado del proyecto y control del demonio. Lo usan la interfaz y los scripts (sin TensorFlow)."""\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\n\nimport psutil\n\nfrom .dataset import clip_files, load_splits\nfrom .paths import (COMMAND_FILE, LABELS_FILE, LANDMARKS, LOG_FILE, MODEL_FILE,\n                    PID_FILE, RAW_VIDEOS, ROOT, RUNTIME, SCRIPTS, SPLITS_FILE, STATUS_FILE,\n                    STOP_FLAG, TEST_RESULTS_FILE)\n\nVIDEO_EXT = {".mp4", ".avi", ".mov", ".mkv", ".webm"}\n\n\ndef read_json(path):\n    try:\n        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:\n            return json.load(f)\n    except (OSError, ValueError):\n        return None\n\n\ndef write_json_atomic(path, data):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + ".tmp")\n    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        json.dump(data, f)\n    os.replace(tmp, path)\n\n\n# ---------------- dataset ----------------\ndef pending_videos(gesture):\n    d = RAW_VIDEOS / gesture\n    if not d.exists():\n        return []\n    return [v for v in sorted(d.iterdir())\n            if v.suffix.lower() in VIDEO_EXT and not (LANDMARKS / gesture / f"{v.stem}.done").exists()]\n\n\ndef dataset_status(settings):\n    splits = load_splits()\n    rows = []\n    for g in settings["gestures"]:\n        counts, unsplit = {"train": 0, "val": 0, "test": 0}, 0\n        files = clip_files(g)\n        for f in files:\n            sp = splits.get(f"{g}/{f.name}")\n            if sp in counts:\n                counts[sp] += 1\n            else:\n                unsplit += 1\n        rows.append({"gesture": g, "clips": len(files), **counts, "unsplit": unsplit,\n                     "pending_videos": len(pending_videos(g))})\n    return rows\n\n\ndef readiness(settings, cam=None):\n    """Lista de (nombre, ok, detalle, requerido) y bandera global de \'listo\'."""\n    rows = dataset_status(settings)\n    minc = settings["dataset"]["min_clips_per_gesture"]\n    checks = []\n\n    low = [f"{r[\'gesture\']} {r[\'clips\']}/{minc}" for r in rows if r["clips"] < minc]\n    checks.append(("Datos de gestos", not low,\n                   "suficientes" if not low else "faltan clips → " + ", ".join(low), True))\n\n    vids = sum(r["pending_videos"] for r in rows)\n    checks.append(("Videos por importar", vids == 0,\n                   "ninguno pendiente" if vids == 0 else f"{vids} video(s) sin importar", False))\n\n    bad = [r["gesture"] for r in rows\n           if r["unsplit"] or min(r["train"], r["val"], r["test"]) < 1]\n    ok_split = SPLITS_FILE.exists() and not bad\n    checks.append(("Train / val / test", ok_split,\n                   "dividido" if ok_split else "falta (re)construir el dataset → "\n                   + (", ".join(bad) if bad else "sin splits"), True))\n\n    labels = read_json(LABELS_FILE)\n    ok_model = MODEL_FILE.exists() and bool(labels) and labels.get("gestures") == settings["gestures"]\n    detail = "entrenado" if ok_model else "sin entrenar (o los gestos cambiaron)"\n    if ok_model and SPLITS_FILE.exists() and SPLITS_FILE.stat().st_mtime > MODEL_FILE.stat().st_mtime:\n        detail += " · el dataset es más nuevo que el modelo: conviene reentrenar"\n    checks.append(("Modelo", ok_model, detail, True))\n\n    res = read_json(TEST_RESULTS_FILE)\n    checks.append(("Test", bool(res),\n                   f"accuracy {res[\'accuracy\']:.1%} en {res[\'n_test\']} clips" if res else "sin evaluar",\n                   False))\n\n    if cam is None:\n        checks.append(("Cámara", False, "sin verificar", False))\n    else:\n        checks.append(("Cámara", cam[0], cam[1], False))\n\n    ready = all(ok for _, ok, _, req in checks if req)\n    return checks, ready\n\n\ndef camera_check(settings):\n    if daemon_pid():\n        return True, "en uso por el demonio"\n    try:\n        from .camera import open_camera\n        cap = open_camera(settings)\n        ok, _ = cap.read()\n        cap.release()\n        return (True, f"cámara {settings[\'camera\'][\'index\']} disponible") if ok else (False, "no entrega imagen")\n    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n        return False, str(e)\n\n\n# ---------------- demonio ----------------\ndef daemon_pid():\n    try:\n        pid = int(PID_FILE.read_text().strip())\n    except (OSError, ValueError):\n        return None\n    try:\n        p = psutil.Process(pid)\n        if p.is_running() and p.status() != psutil.STATUS_ZOMBIE and any(\n                "run.py" in part for part in p.cmdline()):\n            return pid\n    except (psutil.NoSuchProcess, psutil.AccessDenied):\n        pass\n    return None\n\n\ndef start_daemon(dry_run=False, preview=False):\n    if daemon_pid():\n        return daemon_pid()\n    RUNTIME.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    STOP_FLAG.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    write_json_atomic(COMMAND_FILE, {"dry_run": bool(dry_run)})\n    cmd = [sys.executable, str(SCRIPTS / "run.py")]\n    if dry_run:\n        cmd.append("--dry-run")\n    if preview:\n        cmd.append("--preview")\n    kw = {"stdin": subprocess.DEVNULL, "cwd": str(ROOT)}\n    if os.name == "nt":\n        kw["creationflags"] = (subprocess.DETACHED_PROCESS | subprocess.CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP\n                               | subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW)\n    else:\n        kw["start_new_session"] = True\n    with open(LOG_FILE, "w", encoding="utf-8") as log:\n        proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, **kw)\n    return proc.pid\n\n\ndef stop_daemon(timeout=6.0):\n    pid = daemon_pid()\n    if not pid:\n        return False\n    RUNTIME.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    STOP_FLAG.write_text("stop")\n    t0 = time.time()\n    while time.time() - t0 < timeout:\n        if not daemon_pid():\n            return True\n        time.sleep(0.2)\n    try:\n        psutil.Process(pid).terminate()\n    except psutil.Error:\n        pass\n    return True\n\n\ndef read_daemon_status():\n    st = read_json(STATUS_FILE)\n    if not st or not daemon_pid():\n        return None\n    return st\n\n\ndef write_command(**kw):\n    write_json_atomic(COMMAND_FILE, kw)\n',
    'src/gesture_control/training.py': '"""Entrenamiento del clasificador."""\nimport json\nimport os\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom .dataset import load_xy\nfrom .features import FEAT_DIM\nfrom .paths import HISTORY_FILE, LABELS_FILE, MODEL_FILE, MODELS\n\n\ndef train(settings):\n    os.environ.setdefault("TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL", "2")\n    import tensorflow as tf\n    from sklearn.utils.class_weight import compute_class_weight\n    from tensorflow import keras\n\n    from .model import build_model\n\n    tr = settings["training"]\n    gestures = settings["gestures"]\n    steps = settings["sequence"]["steps"]\n    np.random.seed(settings["dataset"].get("seed", 42))\n    tf.random.set_seed(settings["dataset"].get("seed", 42))\n\n    Xtr, ytr = load_xy(settings, "train", augment=True, seed=1)\n    Xva, yva = load_xy(settings, "val", augment=False)\n    if len(Xtr) == 0 or len(Xva) == 0:\n        raise SystemExit("Faltan datos de train/val. Graba clips y ejecuta build_dataset.py primero.")\n    missing = [g for i, g in enumerate(gestures) if not (ytr == i).any()]\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(f"Sin datos de entrenamiento para: {\', \'.join(missing)}")\n    print(f"train: {len(Xtr)} muestras (con aumento) · val: {len(Xva)} · clases: {len(gestures)}", flush=True)\n\n    classes = np.arange(len(gestures))\n    w = compute_class_weight("balanced", classes=classes, y=ytr)\n    model = build_model(steps, FEAT_DIM, len(gestures))\n    cbs = [\n        keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(monitor="val_loss", patience=10, restore_best_weights=True),\n        keras.callbacks.ReduceLROnPlateau(monitor="val_loss", factor=0.5, patience=4, min_lr=1e-5),\n    ]\n    hist = model.fit(Xtr, ytr, validation_data=(Xva, yva), epochs=int(tr["epochs"]),\n                     batch_size=int(tr["batch_size"]), class_weight=dict(zip(classes, w)),\n                     callbacks=cbs, verbose=2)\n    MODELS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    model.save(MODEL_FILE)\n    with open(LABELS_FILE, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        json.dump({"gestures": gestures, "steps": steps, "feat_dim": FEAT_DIM}, f, indent=1)\n    with open(HISTORY_FILE, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:\n        json.dump({k: [float(v) for v in vals] for k, vals in hist.history.items()\n                   if k in ("loss", "val_loss", "accuracy", "val_accuracy")}, f)\n    best = max(hist.history["val_accuracy"])\n    print(f"\\nModelo guardado en {MODEL_FILE.name}. Mejor val_accuracy: {best:.1%}", flush=True)\n',
}


def main():
    dest = Path(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "gesture-control")
    for d in DIRS:
        (dest / d).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    for rel, text in FILES.items():
        p = dest / rel
        p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        if p.exists():
            print(f"existe, se omite: {rel}")
            continue
        p.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8", newline="\n")
        print(f"creado: {rel}")
    print(f"\nListo. Siguiente: cd {dest} && python -m venv .venv && pip install -r requirements.txt")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
